{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two whole-wheat pita pockets generously stuffed with a vibrant tuna and cannellini bean salad, centered in the frame with ample negative space. The camera is positioned at a 3/4 overhead angle, ensuring the textures of the chunky white bean mash, flaky light tuna, vibrant diced cucumber, bright red cherry tomato quarters, and sharp purple red onion are clearly visible. The pitas are slightly torn at the edges, showing a soft, rustic whole-wheat interior. Lighting is soft, natural, and directional from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the fresh sheen of olive oil and lemon juice on the salad. The surface is a weathered, light-colored oak kitchen table with subtle grain markings. Props include a rumpled, off-white linen napkin tucked partially under one plate, a few stray bits of chopped fresh parsley scattered naturally on the table, and a half-squeezed lemon resting to the side. The two servings are placed on simple, matte off-white ceramic plates; one plate is sharp in the foreground, the second is slightly blurred in the background. The scene includes authentic, lived-in details: an asymmetric garnish of parsley, a tiny crumb of pita on the table, and a natural, non-uniform distribution of the filling. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry, no hands, no faces, no text."
}
